  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Quinto Fiorentino is a place located in the plain of the Arno River to the west of Florence. Its location corresponds to the fifth mile of the Roman road. The site is especially known for two Etruscan tholos-type tombs a th\u00f2los, one of which is the Tomba della Mula, and the other the Tomba della Montagnola.",
